# MAGIC <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">04</span><span class="sec-icon">🎛️</span><h2>Variables and overrides</h2></div><p>The value of a variable is resolved in this order of precedence (highest first):</p>
# MAGIC <ol>
# MAGIC <li><code>--var="catalog=prod"</code> on the CLI</li>
# MAGIC <li><code>BUNDLE_VAR_catalog</code> environment variable (great for CI secrets)</li>
# MAGIC <li><code>targets.&lt;target&gt;.variables</code></li>
# MAGIC <li>The variable's <code>default</code></li>
# MAGIC </ol>
# MAGIC <ul>
# MAGIC <li>A variable can be a <strong>lookup</strong>, which resolves an ID by name: <code>lookup: { warehouse: "Shared SQL" }</code>.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Never</strong> put credentials in <code>databricks.yml</code>. Inject them through <code>BUNDLE_VAR_…</code>, or use secret scopes.</li>
# MAGIC <li>Bundle variables are <strong>deployment-time</strong> values. Values that change <strong>per run</strong> belong in <strong>job parameters</strong>.</li>
# MAGIC </ul>
# MAGIC </div>

